    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d42">

                <pb facs="0070" n="44" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v5/pg44"/>

                <head>No. 35.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#center">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Extract from the speech of Mr. Calhoun</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">of South Carolina</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">in
                            the Senate</hi>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1846-03-16"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">March</hi> 16, 1846</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>* * * “The past history of the affair, the fact that it had been frequently
                    offered by us substantially as an ultimatum, added to the fact that 49° was the
                    boundary on this side of the Rocky Mountains, left no doubt on my mind that, if
                    settled by compromise, it must be on that basis.” * * * *<seg type="margin">The
                        line of 49° the only line admissible.</seg></p>
            </div>
        </body>
